{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.VolThroughTau","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.VolThroughTau","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Kashaev"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.vol_through_tau_of_volumeConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.vol_through_tau_of_volumeConjecture","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vol-through-tau.lean#L66-L87","doc":"**Vol(K) factors through τ (conditional on the Kashaev volume\nconjecture).**\n\nHypotheses:\n* `[VolumeConjecture q]` — the class axiomatisation of\n  `conj:kashaev-volume-conjecture`: the hyperbolic volume equals\n  the Kashaev limit (`kvc_holds`).\n* `hcomp` — the computation rule of the archimedean realization\n  functor: `τ_arch` evaluates the algebraic quantum volume\n  `Vol_q(β)` as the Kashaev limit of `β` (per\n  `def:archimedean-realization-functor`).\n\nConclusion: the real-valued knot volume factors through the fibre\nfunctor, `Vol(K_β) = τ_arch(Vol_q(β))` — derived from `kvc_holds`,\nnot assumed. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:vol-through-tau","label":"prop:vol-through-tau","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vol-through-tau.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor.archRestriction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor.archRestriction","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vol-through-tau.lean#L60-L64","doc":"The archimedean restriction `τ_arch = π_∞ ∘ τ`, derived from `τ.functor`\nand `Arch.archProj`. A plain function `C → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor.functor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor.functor","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vol-through-tau.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The underlying genuine functor `τ : C ⥤ Arch.Obj`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vol-through-tau.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor","kind":"structure","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vol-through-tau.lean#L39-L58","doc":"The QOU **fibre functor** `τ`, a genuine `C ⥤ Arch.Obj`.\n\nBrought into line with the library declaration\n(`lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean:102`), which is ahead of this mirror on\nboth counts (bean `qou-u87j`):\n\n* this had `obj : C → Arch.Obj` — an action on **objects only**, with no\n  action on morphisms and no functor laws. A structure named\n  `FibreFunctor` that is not a functor.\n* `archRestriction` was a **free field**, so \"the archimedean restriction\n  `τ_arch = π_∞ ∘ τ`\" could be any function `C → ℝ` unrelated to `τ`. It\n  is now *derived*, which is what its own docstring always claimed.\n\n`archRestriction` is deliberately not a functor: it composes `τ` with the\nobject-level evaluation `Arch.archProj`, and its codomain `ℝ` is a ring,\nnot a category. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.archProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.archProj","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vol-through-tau.lean#L35-L35","doc":"Real-valued evaluation `π_∞ : Obj → ℝ` on the archimedean place\n(object-level; not functorial). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.cat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.cat","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vol-through-tau.lean#L32-L32","doc":"The category structure on `Arch` — morphisms, composition, identities.\nThis is what makes `τ : C ⥤ Arch.Obj` a genuine functor, and it is what\nthis mirror was missing (bean `qou-u87j`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.Obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.Obj","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vol-through-tau.lean#L28-L28","doc":"Carrier type of objects in `Arch`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.mk","kind":"ctor","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vol-through-tau.lean#L26-L26","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory","kind":"structure","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vol-through-tau.lean#L24-L35","doc":"Abstract archimedean target category Arch (e.g. smooth manifolds,\nreal Hilbert spaces, or any chosen archimedean realization). ","signatureChunk":0}]}